# Unbreakable Oracle Modelfile
# This file creates the Unbreakable Oracle model from the llama3.2 base.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Download the GGUF: (or skip this step if you already have llama3.2)
#      curl -L -o unbreakable-oracle.gguf https://simplebeacon.ai/models/unbreakable-oracle.gguf
#
#   2. Create the model:
#      ollama create unbreakable-oracle -f Modelfile
#
#   3. Run it:
#      ollama run unbreakable-oracle
#
# Alternative (if you already have llama3.2 installed):
#   Replace the FROM line below with:
#   FROM llama3.2
#
# Context window: 8192 tokens (matches context-window-chunker default)
# Without PARAMETER num_ctx, Ollama defaults to 2048 tokens, which silently
# truncates the chunked prompts produced by the SimpleBeacon orchestrator.
#
# Quantization: Q4_K_M (4.84 bits/weight) — recommended balance for production.
# ~4.4 GB VRAM for 7B models, minimal quality loss vs FP16.
# For constrained hardware, use the minimal profile (see memory-profiles.json).
# For maximum quality, use Q5_K_M (~5.1 GB VRAM, near-negligible quality loss).
#
# GPU offload: num_gpu -1 = auto-detect (Ollama offloads as many layers as fit).
# Set num_gpu 0 for CPU-only inference on machines without a GPU.
# Set num_gpu 999 to force maximum GPU offload when Ollama under-detects VRAM.

FROM llama3.2:3b-instruct-q4_K_M

TEMPLATE """<|start_header_id|>system<|end_header_id|>

Cutting Knowledge Date: December 2023

You are The Unbreakable Oracle - Reality's Immune System.

{{- if .Tools }}When you receive a tool call response, use the output to format an answer to the orginal user question.

You are a helpful assistant with tool calling capabilities.
{{- end }}<|eot_id|>
{{- range $i, $_ := .Messages }}
{{- $last := eq (len (slice $.Messages $i)) 1 }}
{{- if eq .Role "user" }}<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>
{{- if and $.Tools $last }}

Given the following functions, please respond with a JSON for a function call with its proper arguments that best answers the given prompt.

Respond in the format {"name": function name, "parameters": dictionary of argument name and its value}. Do not use variables.

{{ range $.Tools }}
{{- . }}
{{ end }}
{{ .Content }}<|eot_id|>
{{- else }}

{{ .Content }}<|eot_id|>
{{- end }}{{ if $last }}<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>

{{ end }}
{{- else if eq .Role "assistant" }}<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>
{{- if .ToolCalls }}
{{ range $.ToolCalls }}
{"name": "{{ .Function.Name }}", "parameters": {{ .Function.Arguments }}}{{ end }}
{{- else }}

{{ .Content }}
{{- end }}{{ if not $last }}<|eot_id|>{{ end }}
{{- else if eq .Role "tool" }}<|start_header_id|>ipython<|end_header_id|>

{{ .Content }}<|eot_id|>{{ if $last }}<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>

{{ end }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}"""
SYSTEM You are The Unbreakable Oracle - Reality's Immune System. You analyze code for security vulnerabilities, AI-generated content provenance, compliance issues, and quality problems. Provide concise, structured analysis focusing on actionable insights.
PARAMETER stop <|start_header_id|>
PARAMETER stop <|end_header_id|>
PARAMETER stop <|eot_id|>
PARAMETER temperature 0.1
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER num_predict 2048
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1
PARAMETER num_gpu -1
PARAMETER f16_kv true

